{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-14620","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13333","text":"Skill 03 — Capability Composition"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-14622","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13334","text":"How capabilities compose via the "},{"id":"spn-13335","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-13336","text":" operator and "},{"id":"spn-13337","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-13338","text":" pipeline operator. ACI algebra properties, type compatibility, and composition validation."}]}],"id":"blk-14621","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-14623","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13339","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14624","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13340","text":"Why This Matters"}]},{"id":"blk-14625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13341","text":"Composition is the core thesis of the [&] Protocol. Individual capabilities are useful; composed capabilities are powerful. The protocol defines two operators that make composition formal, validated, and portable."}]},{"id":"blk-14626","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13342","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14627","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13343","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-13344","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-13345","text":" Operator — Capability Sets"}]},{"id":"blk-14628","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13346","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-13347","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-13348","text":" operator combines capabilities into a validated set. It is the fundamental composition mechanism."}]},{"id":"blk-14629","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"&memory.graph & &time.anomaly & &reason.argument"},{"id":"blk-14630","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13349","text":"This declares an agent with graph memory, temporal anomaly detection, and structured argumentation — composed as a single unit."}]},{"id":"blk-14631","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13350","text":"ACI Properties"}]},{"id":"blk-14632","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13351","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-13352","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-13353","text":" operator satisfies ACI (Associative, Commutative, Idempotent):"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-14634","spans":[{"id":"spn-13354","text":"Property"}]},{"id":"blk-14635","spans":[{"id":"spn-13355","text":"Meaning"}]},{"id":"blk-14636","spans":[{"id":"spn-13356","text":"Example"}]}],"id":"blk-14633","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-14637","spans":[{"id":"spn-13357","marks":["bold"],"text":"Associative"}]},{"id":"blk-14638","spans":[{"id":"spn-13358","text":"Grouping does not matter"}]},{"id":"blk-14639","spans":[{"id":"spn-13359","marks":["code"],"text":"(&memory & &time) & &space = &memory & (&time & &space)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14640","spans":[{"id":"spn-13360","marks":["bold"],"text":"Commutative"}]},{"id":"blk-14641","spans":[{"id":"spn-13361","text":"Order does not matter"}]},{"id":"blk-14642","spans":[{"id":"spn-13362","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory & &time = &time & &memory"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14643","spans":[{"id":"spn-13363","marks":["bold"],"text":"Idempotent"}]},{"id":"blk-14644","spans":[{"id":"spn-13364","text":"Duplicates collapse"}]},{"id":"blk-14645","spans":[{"id":"spn-13365","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory & &memory = &memory"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14646","spans":[{"id":"spn-13366","marks":["bold"],"text":"Identity"}]},{"id":"blk-14647","spans":[{"id":"spn-13367","text":"Composing with nothing changes nothing"}]},{"id":"blk-14648","spans":[{"id":"spn-13368","marks":["code"],"text":"&none & &memory = &memory"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-14649","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13369","text":"These are the same properties CRDTs use for conflict-free convergence. They ensure capability sets are deterministic regardless of declaration order."}]},{"id":"blk-14650","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13370","text":"Composition validation"}]},{"id":"blk-14651","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13371","text":"When you run "},{"id":"spn-13372","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand compose"},{"id":"spn-13373","text":", the tool checks:"}]},{"id":"blk-14652","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13374","text":"1. All capability identifiers are valid ("},{"id":"spn-13375","marks":["code"],"text":"&primitive.subtype"},{"id":"spn-13376","text":") 2. All referenced providers exist in the registry (or are "},{"id":"spn-13377","marks":["code"],"text":"\"auto\""},{"id":"spn-13378","text":") 3. No conflicting providers for the same capability 4. ACI properties hold (duplicate removal, order normalization)"}]},{"id":"blk-14653","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13379","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14654","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13380","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-13381","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-13382","text":" Operator — Pipelines"}]},{"id":"blk-14655","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13383","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-13384","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-13385","text":" operator flows data through capability operations in sequence:"}]},{"id":"blk-14656","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"stream_data\n  |> &time.anomaly.detect()\n  |> &memory.graph.enrich()\n  |> &reason.argument.evaluate()"},{"id":"blk-14657","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13386","text":"Each step receives the output of the previous step as input. The pipeline is type-checked against capability contracts."}]},{"id":"blk-14658","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13387","text":"Type Compatibility"}]},{"id":"blk-14659","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13388","text":"Pipelines are validated using "},{"id":"spn-13389","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-13390","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-13391","marks":["code"],"text":"feeds_into"},{"id":"spn-13392","text":" contracts:"}]},{"id":"blk-14660","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Step 1: &time.anomaly.detect()\n  Input:  stream_data\n  Output: anomaly_set\n\nStep 2: &memory.graph.enrich()\n  Accepts: anomaly_set (via &time.* wildcard in accepts_from)\n  Output:  enriched_context\n\nStep 3: &reason.argument.evaluate()\n  Accepts: enriched_context (via &memory.* wildcard in accepts_from)\n  Output:  evaluation_result"},{"id":"blk-14661","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13393","text":"If Step N's output type does not match Step N+1's "},{"id":"spn-13394","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"},{"id":"spn-13395","text":" list, composition fails with a type error."}]},{"id":"blk-14662","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13396","text":"Wildcard matching"}]},{"id":"blk-14663","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13397","text":"Contract types support wildcard matching:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-14665","spans":[{"id":"spn-13398","text":"Pattern"}]},{"id":"blk-14666","spans":[{"id":"spn-13399","text":"Matches"}]}],"id":"blk-14664","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-14667","spans":[{"id":"spn-13400","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory.*"}]},{"id":"blk-14668","spans":[{"id":"spn-13401","text":"Any memory capability output"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14669","spans":[{"id":"spn-13402","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason.*"}]},{"id":"blk-14670","spans":[{"id":"spn-13403","text":"Any reasoning capability output"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14671","spans":[{"id":"spn-13404","marks":["code"],"text":"raw_data"}]},{"id":"blk-14672","spans":[{"id":"spn-13405","text":"Literal type "},{"id":"spn-13406","marks":["code"],"text":"raw_data"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14673","spans":[{"id":"spn-13407","marks":["code"],"text":"output"}]},{"id":"blk-14674","spans":[{"id":"spn-13408","text":"Terminal — pipeline result"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-14675","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13409","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14676","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13410","text":"Pipeline Declarations in JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-14677","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13411","text":"Pipelines are declared in the "},{"id":"spn-13412","marks":["code"],"text":"pipelines"},{"id":"spn-13413","text":" block of "},{"id":"spn-13414","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-13415","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-14678","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"\"pipelines\": {\n  \"incident_triage\": {\n    \"source_type\": \"stream_data\",\n    \"source_ref\": \"raw_data\",\n    \"steps\": [\n      { \"capability\": \"&time.anomaly\", \"operation\": \"detect\" },\n      { \"capability\": \"&memory.graph\", \"operation\": \"enrich\" },\n      { \"capability\": \"&reason.argument\", \"operation\": \"evaluate\" }\n    ]\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14679","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13416","text":"Each step references a capability declared in the "},{"id":"spn-13417","marks":["code"],"text":"capabilities"},{"id":"spn-13418","text":" block and an operation defined in that capability's contract."}]},{"id":"blk-14680","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13419","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14681","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13420","text":"Multi-Capability Declarations"}]},{"id":"blk-14682","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13421","text":"An agent can declare any combination of capabilities across all four primitive domains:"}]},{"id":"blk-14683","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"\"capabilities\": {\n  \"&memory.graph\":      { \"provider\": \"graphonomous\", \"config\": {} },\n  \"&memory.vector\":     { \"provider\": \"pgvector\", \"config\": {} },\n  \"&time.anomaly\":      { \"provider\": \"ticktickclock\", \"config\": {} },\n  \"&time.forecast\":     { \"provider\": \"ticktickclock\", \"config\": {} },\n  \"&space.fleet\":       { \"provider\": \"geofleetic\", \"config\": {} },\n  \"&reason.argument\":   { \"provider\": \"deliberatic\", \"config\": {} },\n  \"&reason.deliberate\": { \"provider\": \"graphonomous\", \"config\": {} }\n}"},{"id":"blk-14684","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13422","text":"Multiple subtypes of the same primitive are allowed. Each is independently bound to a provider."}]},{"id":"blk-14685","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13423","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14686","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13424","text":"Composition Validation via CLI"}]},{"id":"blk-14687","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"./ampersand compose agent.ampersand.json"},{"id":"blk-14688","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13425","marks":["bold"],"text":"Success output:"}]},{"id":"blk-14689","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OK  agent.ampersand.json\n  Capability set: &memory.graph & &time.anomaly & &reason.argument\n  ACI normal form: &memory.graph & &reason.argument & &time.anomaly\n  Pipelines: incident_triage (3 steps, type-safe)\n  Providers: graphonomous, ticktickclock, deliberatic"},{"id":"blk-14690","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13426","marks":["bold"],"text":"Failure output:"}]},{"id":"blk-14691","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"FAIL  agent.ampersand.json\n  errors:\n    - Pipeline \"incident_triage\" step 2: &memory.graph.enrich() does not\n      accept type \"forecast_set\" (output of &time.forecast.predict())\n    - Provider \"unknown_service\" not found in registry"},{"id":"blk-14692","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13427","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14693","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13428","text":"Anti-Patterns"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-14695","spans":[{"id":"spn-13429","text":"Anti-Pattern"}]},{"id":"blk-14696","spans":[{"id":"spn-13430","text":"Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-14697","spans":[{"id":"spn-13431","text":"Fix"}]}],"id":"blk-14694","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-14698","spans":[{"id":"spn-13432","text":"Incompatible pipeline steps"}]},{"id":"blk-14699","spans":[{"id":"spn-13433","text":"Output type does not match next step's "},{"id":"spn-13434","marks":["code"],"text":"accepts_from"}]},{"id":"blk-14700","spans":[{"id":"spn-13435","text":"Check contracts; insert a compatible intermediary"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14701","spans":[{"id":"spn-13436","text":"Circular pipeline dependencies"}]},{"id":"blk-14702","spans":[{"id":"spn-13437","text":"`"}]},{"id":"blk-14703","spans":[{"id":"spn-13438","text":">` is strictly linear"}]},{"id":"blk-14704","spans":[{"id":"spn-13439","text":"Use capability-level feedback, not pipeline cycles"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14705","spans":[{"id":"spn-13440","text":"Composing without validating"}]},{"id":"blk-14706","spans":[{"id":"spn-13441","text":"Errors surface late at generation time"}]},{"id":"blk-14707","spans":[{"id":"spn-13442","text":"Always "},{"id":"spn-13443","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-13444","text":" before "},{"id":"spn-13445","marks":["code"],"text":"generate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14708","spans":[{"id":"spn-13446","text":"Ignoring ACI normalization"}]},{"id":"blk-14709","spans":[{"id":"spn-13447","text":"Assuming order matters when it does not"}]},{"id":"blk-14710","spans":[{"id":"spn-13448","text":"Trust the normal form; do not rely on declaration order"}]}],[{"id":"blk-14711","spans":[{"id":"spn-13449","text":"Over-composing"}]},{"id":"blk-14712","spans":[{"id":"spn-13450","text":"Declaring 15 capabilities when 3 suffice"}]},{"id":"blk-14713","spans":[{"id":"spn-13451","text":"Start minimal; add capabilities when needed"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-14714","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13452","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-14715","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-13453","text":"Elixir DSL Equivalent"}]},{"id":"blk-14716","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13454","text":"In the Elixir reference implementation, composition uses native syntax:"}]},{"id":"blk-14717","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"capabilities do\n  &memory.graph(:graphonomous, instance: \"infra-ops\")\n  &time.anomaly(:ticktickclock, streams: [:cpu, :mem])\n  &reason.argument(:deliberatic, governance: :constitutional)\nend"},{"id":"blk-14718","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13455","text":"Pipeline usage:"}]},{"id":"blk-14719","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"stream_data\n|> &time.anomaly.detect()\n|> &memory.graph.enrich()\n|> &reason.argument.evaluate()"},{"id":"blk-14720","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-13456","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-13457","marks":["code"],"text":"&"},{"id":"spn-13458","text":" leverages Elixir's capture operator. The "},{"id":"spn-13459","marks":["code"],"text":"|>"},{"id":"spn-13460","text":" is Elixir's native pipe. Both map directly to the protocol's formal operators."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierajva6ydyvbnawu2xkhk4d57ogktbk5r67fclzzvgfngoa52uuvxaa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}